{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"A Cup of Rice: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja5'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 5 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sure Bet </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>5. Taṇḍulanāḷijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A Cup of Rice: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kimagghati taṇḍulanāḷikāyaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Speak, O King: what value has a cup of rice </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Assāna mūlāya vadehi rāja; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for the pricing of horses?” </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bārāṇasiṁ santarabāhirantaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“He values a cup of rice </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ayamagghati taṇḍulanāḷikā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>at Varanasi with its suburbs!” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Taṇḍulanāḷijātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
